E-APACHE】  | 【88†LICENSE-APACHE】  |    |\nL200: 【89†LICENSE-MIT】  | 【89†LICENSE-MIT】  |    |\nL201: 【90†README.md】  | 【90†README.md】  |    |\nL202: ## Repository files navigation\nL203: \nL204:   *   * 【91†README】\nL205:   * 【91†Apache-2.0 license】\nL206:   * 【91†MIT license】\nL207: \nL208: More items\nL209: # Linear-Time Sumcheck\nL210: \nL211: `linear-sumcheck` is a Rust library that implements the sumcheck protocol.\nL212: \nL213: This crate implements the following protocols:\nL214: \nL215:   * 【92†`MLSumcheck`】: The sumcheck protocol for products of multilinear polynomials in evaluation form over boolean hypercube.\nL216:   * 【93†`GKRRoundSumcheck`】: The sumcheck protocol for GKR Round Function. This protocol takes `MLSumcheck` as a subroutine.\nL217: WARNING: This is an academic proof-of-concept prototype, and in particular has not received careful code review. This implementation is NOT ready for production use.\nL218: ## Build guide\nL219: \nL220: The library compiles on the `stable` toolchain of the Rust compiler. To install the latest version of Rust, first install `rustup` by following the instructions 【94†here†rustup.rs】, or via your platform's package manager. Once `rustup` is installed, install the Rust toolchain by invoking:\nL221: \nL222:     rustup install stable\nL223: After that, use `cargo` (the standard Rust build tool) to build the library:\nL224: \nL225:     git clone https://github.com/arkworks-rs/sumcheck.git\nL226:     cd sumcheck\nL227:     cargo build --release\nL228: \nL229: This library comes with some unit and integration tests. Run these tests with:\nL230: \nL231:     cargo test\nL232: \nL233: Lastly, this library is instrumented with profiling infrastructure that prints detailed traces of execution time. To enable this, compile with `cargo build --features print-trace`.\nL234: ## Benchmarks\nL235: \nL236: To run the benchmarks, install the nightly Rust toolchain, via `rustup install nightly`, and then run the following command:\nL237: \nL238:     cargo +nightly bench --all-features\nL239: \nL240: All benchmarks below are performed over BLS12-381 scalar field implemented in the `ark-test-curves` library. Benchmarks were run on a machine with an Intel Xeon 6136 CPU running at 3.0 GHz.\nL241: \nL242: #### Benchmarks for `MLSumcheck`\nL243: \nL244: #### Benchmarks for `GKRRoundSumcheck`\nL245: ## License\nL246: \nL247: This library is licensed under either of the following licenses, at your discretion.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReleases · arkworks-rs/sumcheck · GitHub (https://github.com/arkworks-rs/sumcheck/releases)\nciteturn2view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/arkworks-rs/sumcheck/releases\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 244\nL0: 【0†Skip to content】\nL1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Sign in】\nL4: \nL5: Appearance settings\nL6: \nL7:   * Platform\nL8: \nL9:     * AI CODE CREATION\nL10:       * 【2†GitHub CopilotWrite better code with AI】\nL11:       * 【3†GitHub Copilot appDirect agents from issue to merge】\nL12:       * 【4†MCP RegistryIntegrate external tools】\nL13: \nL14:     * DEVELOPER WORKFLOWS\nL15:       * 【5†ActionsAutomate any workflow】\nL16:       * 【6†CodespacesInstant dev environments】\nL17:       * 【7†IssuesPlan and track work】\nL18:       * 【8†Code ReviewManage code changes】\nL19:       * 【9†Code QualityEnforce quality at merge】\nL20:     * APPLICATION SECURITY\nL21:       * 【10†GitHub Advanced SecurityFind and fix vulnerabilities】\nL22:       * 【11†Code securitySecure your code as you build】\nL23:       * 【12†Secret protectionStop leaks before they start】\nL24: \nL25:     * EXPLORE\nL26:       * 【13†Why GitHub】\nL27:       * 【14†Documentation†docs.github.com】\nL28:       * 【15†Blog†github.blog】\nL29:       * 【16†Changelog†github.blog】\nL30:       * 【17†Marketplace】\nL31: \nL32: 【18†View all features】\nL33: \nL34:   * Solutions\nL35:     * BY